WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.050
Picture a bus that runs
all day on hydrogen.

2
00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:06.850
There's no engine roaring,
and nothing is burning.

3
00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:10.810
Yet it has all the electricity
it needs to drive its motors.

4
00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:14.670
And the only thing coming out
of its exhaust pipe is water.

5
00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:17.970
Hydrogen goes in, oxygen
from the air goes in,

6
00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:19.850
and water comes out.

7
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:22.690
So how does that reaction
make electricity?

8
00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:26.170
In this mission, you'll see
how chemicals reacting inside a

9
00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:27.920
cell can produce electricity.

10
00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:30.070
You'll meet the hydrogen fuel cell,

11
00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:33.030
and the overall reaction
that powers it.

12
00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:37.210
Your mission: explain how a fuel
cell turns hydrogen and oxygen

13
00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:38.990
into electricity.
